======================================================================================
(3) MECHANISM: WHY N-1 is removed, and the even-branch better-t
======================================================================================
  At binding maximizer a=3*inv5 mod q (q=3N+2): 3(N-1)=q-5 == -5, so
  (N-1)*a = (N-1)*3*inv5 = [3(N-1)]*inv5 = -5*inv5 = -1 mod q.
  => speed N-1 is ALWAYS at residue -1 (dist 1) -- FORCED collision, hence
     removed.  The mediant lower bound M >= 3/q holds for ALL N (this t).

  The trichotomy is about the GLOBAL max.  For N even, a t at Q=3N-1 beats
  the mediant.  Binding at that t (N even):
    N=8: Q=3N-1=23, max t=10/23, min=3/23; binding [(2, 3), (21, 3)]
    N=12: Q=3N-1=35, max t=16/35, min=3/35; binding [(2, 3), (33, 3)]
    N=14: Q=3N-1=41, max t=19/41, min=3/41; binding [(2, 3), (39, 3)]

  For N==1 mod 6, NO t beats the mediant => M = 3/(3N+2), the gap member.
  For N==3,5 mod 6, the max is 1/N (the far element + parity leave 1/N open).
